this was coventry hospital at the peak  of the pandemic hospitals in england  were then admitting over 4 000 patients  a day  that number could be dwarfed this winter  according to government scientists who  have  their worst case scenario we've seen a  steady rise over recent weeks although  it has plateaued over recent days  the chief executive of coventry hospital  professor andy hardy told me those  numbers can't be ignored  but he's confident  his hospitals can cope with more  patients than in previous waves  it's fair to say that uh all of us are  always concerned about every winter that  comes up what we all do in the health  service is  you know we  we plan and prepare for the worst and  hope for the best we're expecting a  tough winter um but whatever comes our  way we intend to deal with it right now  the nhs is admitting around 1 000 new  covered patients each day that's much  higher than at this time last year they  peaked at around four and a half  thousand in january in 2021. the latest  modeling says admissions could rise to  between two and seven thousand this year  cases are increasing hospitalizations  are increasing  professor ko is a member of spymo the  panel of scientists that produced this  modeling  you have been wrong in the past  kind of projection that you have is  never going to be an exact crystal ball  so no matter what happens we always need  to plan on the basis of what we think  may happen now what we think may happen  can always be wrong the health secretary  said previous modeling predictions had  not come true but accepts some  mitigation measures may be needed  what happens in the nhs is going to be  hugely important to me to the whole  country making sure that we don't get to  a position again where the nhs becomes  unsustainable of course that would be  the level of hospitalization it will be  the pressures on a e the pressures on  the workforce so we'd have to take all  of these together  much has changed we have the vaccine and  better pandemic preparedness  but this is our first winter with the  delta variant the only thing we can say  with any certainty is that this winter  is going to be tough  joshi sky news
 

